  "dom_id": "step-q81856",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  .",
  "worked_solution": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 7-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
